#
# Production inference dependencies for Kimodo MCP Server — third-party only.
#
# Compile the lockfile (do NOT run `uv pip compile` by hand — the pinned versions must
# be resolved against the PyTorch index and for linux/py3.10, not for whatever machine
# you happen to be on):
#   python kimodo/scripts/lock_requirements.py --prod
#
# That writes `docker_requirements_prod.txt`, which IS committed and IS what
# Dockerfile.base installs (with --no-deps, so the lockfile is the only authority).
#
# NOTE: torch is listed here because prod uses a minimal CUDA base image instead of the
# NGC PyTorch image, so nothing else supplies it. Its cu124 wheels bundle their own
# cuBLAS/cuDNN/cuFFT under site-packages/nvidia — that is why the runtime stage can sit
# on `nvidia/cuda:...-base` rather than `...-runtime`.
#
# Local packages (`./MotionCorrection`, `.`) are deliberately NOT listed here. They are
# built explicitly in Dockerfile.base — MotionCorrection needs a C++ toolchain, and
# kimodo is built as a wheel rather than installed editable.
#

# PyTorch
torch>=2.1.0

# Config
hydra-core>=1.3
omegaconf>=2.3

# Core numerics
